# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party source material. NOT committed, deliberately.
#
# ref/ holds Dajo Energy Limited's company profile. That is a DIFFERENT
# company's document. It was used as a structural and tonal reference only,
# and none of its facts appear on this site. Committing it would republish
# another company's material under Terk's name, and git history is difficult
# to scrub once pushed.
#
# Nothing in ref/ is needed to build or run the site: the logo is already at
# assets/img/terk-mark.png and the contact details are in includes/config.php.
#
# If you decide you do want it tracked, delete the next line, but check first
# that this repository is private and that you are entitled to redistribute it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ref/

# Local tooling. Machine-specific absolute paths, not portable.
/.claude/
/.remember/
/.playwright-mcp/

# Review artefacts: screenshots and concept sketches from the build.
/.impeccable/shots/
/.impeccable/sketches/

# The design system record IS tracked; it documents the built site.
!/.impeccable/design.json

# Local mail capture, if TERK_MAIL_SINK is ever pointed inside the project.
*.mail.log
terk-mail*.log

# OS and editor noise
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Decision-page logs from the design session, not project files.
/.impeccable/questions/

# Live mail credentials. The template (mail-config.example.php) IS tracked;
# the filled-in copy never is, and belongs above the web root anyway.
/mail-config.php
mail-config.php

# Mail failure log written by send.php
terk-mail-errors.log
